-- title:
--   Frobenius-semilinear transport of differentials preserving pole orders
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $p$, let $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ have finite index and contain the translation matrix $T$, and write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of reductions of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma$ (denominator nonzero). The assertion is the existence of an additive endomorphism $\sigma_\Omega$ of the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ with three properties. First, $p$-semilinearity over $K$: $\sigma_\Omega(a\omega) = a^p\,\sigma_\Omega(\omega)$ for all $a \in K$. Second, on $q$-expansions of differentials, taken through the $F$-linear map [`ModularCurve.diffQExp`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeDifferential.html#L128) attached to the derivation $q\,d/dq$ restricted to $F$, the operator raises coefficients to the $p$-th power without changing their index: the $n$-th coefficient of the expansion of $\sigma_\Omega(\omega)$ is the $p$-th power of the $n$-th coefficient of that of $\omega$, for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$. Third, pole orders are transported to the place pulled back along the $q$-expansion Frobenius: for every place $v$ of $F$ over $K$ (a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, proper, and a principal ideal ring), every $\omega$, every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and every $f \in F$, if $\omega = f\cdot d\pi_v$ for the chosen uniformiser $\pi_v$ of $v$ and $\pi_v^n f$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$, then there is $g \in F$ with $\sigma_\Omega(\omega) = g \cdot d\pi_{w}$ and $\pi_{w}^n g$ in the valuation subring of $w$, where $w =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL K Γ p v`](def/ModularCurve_QExpFrobeniusModL.html#L132) is the restriction of $v$ along the $K$-algebra endomorphism [`ModularCurve.qExpFrobeniusModL K Γ p`](def/ModularCurve_QExpFrobeniusModL.html#L76) of $F$ induced by the exponent-scaling operation $q \mapsto q^p$ on Laurent series.
--
--   This provides the Frobenius push-forward on differentials of the $q$-expansion function field in characteristic $p$, characterised by coefficientwise $p$-th powers on $q$-expansions, together with the statement that it moves a differential with a pole of order at most $n$ at $v$ to one with a pole of order at most $n$ at the Frobenius pull-back place. It is used, in combination with the Cartier operator, to bound poles of the Frobenius push-forward appearing in the mod $p$ Hecke action on differentials.
